Z||000000||fiero109||02-27-2000||12:51 AM||||need help..my 84 se headlight neither go up or down.already changed out the relays and still nothing...if any of you smart fiero fellows now how to fix it please let me now...thanks<P>wes||||reg||1
Z||000001||AL||02-27-2000||02:21 AM||||did you check the brushes inside the motors?also check fuse,if the relays are good do you hear them click when you move it around, if you don't it's a relay, also check the one in front of the light open her up and check the contacts if the contact is dirty or humid clean it.good luck, AL. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ggarsk||02-27-2000||02:26 AM||||I would definitly check the brushes in the motor. They have a tendency to fall off due to their age.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodney||02-27-2000||08:00 AM||||I have new brush/contact assemblies for the 84-86 headlight actuators. OEM manuufacture. Includes the wiring pig tails with the correct plug in connectors. $21.00 each and $2.00 shipping. The whole assembly just slips into the case thru the opening under the small cover. I also have the OEM gears and internal bumpers. Gears are $20.00 each and the internal bumpers are $0.75 each. Each gear comes with 8 screws and nuts to reassemble the case and a packet of Dow Corning 33 silicone grease. The expensive good grease that will not dry out. With these new parts and a little labor you can make an old acuator like new again. The rest of the parts in the assemblies are very durable. No web page on the 84-86 parts yet. Soon I hope.<P>Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
